      "created_at": "2017-07-29T12:30:55Z",
      "updated_at": "2017-07-29T12:30:55Z",
      "body": "What concerns me is the last part. My location does **not** change significantly when I make photos. However I expect that the app uploads them once I made them and I have seen it uploads more or less directly. I think it is not correct that I need to move 1km to get my photos uploaded, isn't it? If WLAN is active it will be uploaded immediately after the photo has been taken. Correct me if I'm wrong.\r\n\r\nI think this info is _inacurrate_ than or at least misleading. It sounds like I need to move 1km to start the sync. Can you think of other wording for this?\r\n\r\nYour sentence may be technically correct, but it is too technical. Hell - that I'm saying this... normally it cannot be enough technical details to understand how something works. May blame Apple the unfriendly way.\r\n",
